# Annot — environment configuration for builds.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` at the repo root and edit the
# values to match your deployment. `.env.local` is gitignored —
# your overrides stay local. Vite reads these values automatically
# at build time and bakes them into the produced artefacts.
#
# To DEPLOY to the canonical hosted version (`annot.work`), leave
# every variable below commented out — the build falls back to
# `annot.work` defaults.
#
# To SELF-HOST under a different domain, uncomment + edit the
# values below. The corresponding `wrangler.jsonc` files
# (`./wrangler.jsonc`, `packages/marketing/wrangler.jsonc`,
# `packages/docs-site/wrangler.jsonc`, `packages/worker/wrangler.jsonc`)
# also need their `routes` field edited to match your zone — see
# `docs/self-hosting.md` for the full walkthrough.

# ─── PWA (packages/web/) ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Vite's `base` config — the URL path prefix the PWA serves at.
# Default: `/app/` (annot.work's hosted layout puts the PWA at
# `annot.work/app/*`, the marketing site at `annot.work/`, the
# docs at `annot.work/docs/*`).
#
# Self-host examples:
#   - PWA at domain root, no marketing site:   VITE_PWA_BASE=/
#   - PWA under a renamed path:                VITE_PWA_BASE=/editor/
#
# VITE_PWA_BASE=/app/

# ─── Extension (packages/extension/) ──────────────────────────
#
# The full URL where the PWA is served. The extension's service
# worker uses this to open the PWA, query existing PWA tabs, and
# build edit-URLs handed back to the PWA via `?extId=...`.
#
# Default in production builds: `https://annot.work/app`
# Default in dev (`vite dev`): `http://localhost:3000/app`
#
# VITE_ANNOTATION_URL=https://annot.example.com/app

# Origin patterns for the extension's `externally_connectable`
# manifest field. Web pages matching these origins can call
# `chrome.runtime.sendMessage(EXT_ID, ...)`. Self-hosters MUST
# include their PWA's origin here for the PWA to talk to the
# extension.
#
# Format: comma-separated list of Chrome match patterns. Each
# pattern needs a `<scheme>://<host>/<path>` shape (Chrome rejects
# `*` as the scheme).
#
# Default: `https://annot.work/*,http://localhost:3000/*`
#
# Self-host example:
#   VITE_EXT_EXTERNALLY_CONNECTABLE_MATCHES=https://annot.example.com/*,http://localhost:3000/*
#
# VITE_EXT_EXTERNALLY_CONNECTABLE_MATCHES=
